1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,650
Spreadsheets run real money. Suture proves exactly where they break.

2
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:13,747
This is Suture, live in the browser. A SaaS runway model: 21.76 months. One rule: runway must never go negative.

3
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:16,614
Three engines. One graph. No server.

4
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:26,710
Formulas sit next to a Python and NumPy burn projection, which reads a DuckDB SQL table. All three run in WebAssembly, right in your tab.

5
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:32,370
X-Ray draws every dependency, across all three engines.

6
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:48,294
Now: Exorcise Model. Suture fuzzes the inputs through SQL, Python, and formulas. In 2.5 seconds, it finds a counterexample, and shrinks it to the smallest failing inputs.

7
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:57,252
Apply it. Runway drops to -179.88. Status: RAISE NOW. The fracture traces it back through the Python projection.

8
00:00:57,300 --> 00:01:00,660
Copy the replay link, and open it in a fresh page.

9
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:05,416
Same seed. Reproduced, exactly.

10
00:01:08,200 --> 00:01:11,027
Apply it again: the same -179.88.

11
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:21,400
Now, at scale. This audit generates 100,000 orders in DuckDB, then runs NumPy, then plain formulas.

12
00:01:25,700 --> 00:01:28,599
Exorcise again, across all three engines.

13
00:01:29,100 --> 00:01:39,200
It finds a real policy bug: the discount cap is applied to each discount, not to the stacked total. So stacked Hardlines orders lose money.

14
00:01:40,450 --> 00:01:43,059
This link came from Suture's Kiro Crew app.

15
00:01:43,100 --> 00:01:45,838
It opens here, and reproduces exactly.

16
00:01:47,200 --> 00:01:52,130
Apply it: the quote is priced at zero, so the margin divides by zero.

17
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:59,840
The same engine ships as an MCP server on npm. This is a real session, not a mock-up.

18
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:12,610
The audit finds the runway bug again. Then, verify_patch replays that counterexample against my fix, and runs a fresh, 1,000-run audit.

19
00:02:14,300 --> 00:02:18,848
Fixed. Zero regressions. Kiro calls these same tools.

20
00:02:18,850 --> 00:02:22,399
I built Suture in Kiro, spec first: five specs.

21
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:24,640
Steering that Kiro always loads.

22
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:28,984
A hook that reruns the property tests after core edits.

23
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:32,149
A log of real bugs, each with a replayable counterexample.

24
00:02:32,900 --> 00:02:33,936
Custom agents.

25
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:37,700
And the Kiro Crew app.

26
00:02:39,750 --> 00:02:46,367
Suture. Every spreadsheet bug, proven. Try it at suture-nu.vercel.app.
